## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| **Critical** | **7** |
| Medium | 2 |

This is a textbook **coverage-touching** test class. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called, achieving high line-coverage, but almost nothing is actually verified. These tests will pass even if the production code is completely broken.

---

### 🔴 Critical Findings

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (Systemic)

The entire class is designed to touch every method without verifying outcomes. 7 of 10 tests have **zero meaningful assertions**.

#### 2. No Assertions — `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)

```csharp
// BEFORE — proves nothing
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// AFTER — verify the product was persisted
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", stored!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, stored.Price);
```

#### 3. No Assertions — `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)

```csharp
// AFTER — verify price actually changed
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

#### 4. No Assertions — `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)

```csharp
// AFTER — verify product is gone
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

#### 5. No Assertions — `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)

```csharp
// AFTER — verify the count is correct
var count = _catalog.GetProductCount();
Assert.AreEqual(0, count);
```

#### 6. No Assertions — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)

```csharp
// AFTER — verify prices were reduced by 10%
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);
```

#### 7. No Assertions — `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 85)

```csharp
// AFTER — verify the import created the product
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var imported = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(imported);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", imported!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, imported.Price);
